  "Question": "If \\(\\log_{10}(x^2-3x+6)=1,\\) the value of \\(x\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(10\\) or \\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\) or \\(-2\\)",
    "C": "\\(3\\) or \\(-1\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\) or \\(-1\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "A base-10 logarithm equals \\(1\\) precisely when its argument equals \\(10^1=10\\). Thus the equation becomes\n\\[\nx^2-3x+6=10,\n\\]\nor\n\\[\nx^2-3x-4=(x-4)(x+1)=0.\n\\]\nA product is zero only if at least one factor is zero, so \\(x=4\\) or \\(x=-1\\). Both values make the original logarithm argument equal to \\(10>0\\), so both are valid. The answer is \\(\\boxed{4\\text{ or }-1}\\), choice D.",
